Independence statement
-----------------------
swelter is an independent personal open-source project. It is unaffiliated with
any employer or client, contains no proprietary or client material, and was not
built for or on behalf of any government customer. It is not a government system.

Observation data
----------------
Environmental observations published by swelter are released under CC0 1.0
Universal (public-domain dedication); see DATA-LICENSE. The observations are
aggregate environmental measurements only — temperature, humidity, particulate
matter, and derived heat/air-quality indices. They contain no personal
information, no device-as-tracker identifiers, and no field capable of locating
a person. Node locations are the hosting collective's to disclose and are
published snapped to a coarse grid unless a host opts in to a precise location.
